[[0,61057,0,11,0,11,"2015-03-08T06:51:51","zombielordzero","",[],"","Flow Hive: Honey on Tap Directly From Your Beehive","https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/flow-hive-honey-on-tap-directly-from-your-beehive","technology"],[1,88318,0,1,0,1,"2015-03-08T15:53:04","dabork","[e]",[],"<p>Fantastic looking product. I have been following this a bit since it was first announced and it looks like they&#39;re moving on to full production now.</p>\n<p>The reviews seem mostly positive aside from a group of very vocal naysayers in the beekeeping community who have convinced themselves this is a scam meant to prey on people and trick hipsters and soccer moms into thinking they can handle beekeeping as a hobby. Most of the &quot;complaints&quot; are entirely specualtion or are based off a problem that doesn&#39;t exist or that was already addressed by the people making it. I have never seen a group of people get so bitter about something so innocent, and you could tell just by the way they were talking that a lot of these people don&#39;t actually have a problem with the product itself, but instead seem to be bothered by the idea of more people joining their niche little hobby and ruining their secret club mentality.</p>\n<p>If this lowers the barrier of entry to beekeeping even a little bit and encourages even a few people to take up beekeeping and do it responsibly, this product was a success. Bees are one of the most important things in our world right now and they&#39;re not exactly doing the best at this point so we could use as many people helping as we can get. It&#39;s really kind of disgusting to see people so caught up in their own selfishness they would rather block progress and innovation.</p>\n<p>I hope it&#39;s perfect. I hope they sell a million units and nobody has a single complaint and the whole thing goes off without a hitch and 4 years from now we have 3 times the amount of beekeepers in the world that we do now. Just so I can see all those bitter assholes boil with rage that they&#39;re not special little snowflakes any more.</p>"],[1,89430,0,0,0,0,"2015-03-10T12:59:25","COUSCOUS","",[],"<p>NOMNOMNOM!!~!</p>"]]
